Description: routed IPs for Proxmox VE virtual machines
 Routes IPv4 and IPv6 addresses and networks of any prefix length to the
 network devices of virtual machines. The host side gateway addresses are
 configurable; in tap-only mode the tap device is not inserted into the bridge
 at all and becomes a point-to-point L3 link to the guest.
 .
 Routes follow running guests: they are installed on the node the guest runs
 on, moved on live migration and updated immediately on configuration changes,
 ready to be picked up by a routing daemon such as BIRD (protocol 150).
 .
 Adds a Routed IP page to the Datacenter and VM views of the web interface.
